{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"The full run exposed a second test-harness issue: it compared whether `realloc` happened to preserve each library’s address even on growth, which is allocator-history-dependent and not an API output. I’m limiting identity checks to the actual C no-growth predicate and making the serialization mutex recover after a failed test so later tests report real results instead of lock poisoning."}}
